{
  "package": "archive/tar",
  "notes": "archive::tar: Go-shaped Reader/Writer/Header over std::io with USTAR, PAX and GNU formats, long names, PAX time precision, sparse reading (old GNU, PAX 0.0/0.1/1.0) and format selection identical to Go (archives written by Go and Rust are byte-identical); Reader::next_raw returns byte-string headers like Go (Reader::next is the String form), times are SystemTime, ErrInsecurePath is opt-in (GODEBUG=tarinsecurepath=0 or Reader::set_reject_insecure_paths) and carries the header; sparse writing (Writer::write_sparse_header) is an extension because Go's is disabled; set_name_lookup is an extension that lets FileInfoHeader resolve names through rust_stdlib_sys::os::user",
  "symbols": {
    "ErrFieldTooLong": {
