    "FileInfoHeader": {
      "rust": "rust_stdlib::archive::tar::file_info_header",
      "note": "Uname and Gname come from a crate-private /etc/passwd and /etc/group parser plus the current user through $USER, because the root crate has no FFI (ADR 0004); Go asks the C library (always on macOS, on Linux when built with cgo), so any NSS or Open Directory id resolves. tar::set_name_lookup installs other lookups; installing rust_stdlib_sys::os::user::lookup_id and lookup_group_id gives Go's result. Real files are checked against Go by tools/check_archive_api.py.",
      "deviation": "no-ffi-in-root"
